<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="curry-lentil-sweet-pot" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Curry - Lentil Sweet Potato</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell>1 cup dried lentils, rinsed</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 cups water, divided</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 large onion, chopped</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>1 tablespoon olive oil</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 medium carrots, chopped</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 garlic cloves, minced</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 medium sweet potatoes, chopped</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>4 teaspoons curry powder</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{3}{4}</m> teaspoon salt</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> teaspoon pepper</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 medium tomatoes, chopped</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 medium apple, chopped</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 tablespoon brown sugar</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 cups hot cooked brown rice</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          In a small saucepan, combine lentils and 2 cups water; bring to a boil.  Reduce heat; cover and simmer for 20 to 25 minutes or until tender.  Drain.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Meanwhile, in a large saucepan, sauté onion in oil until tender.  Add carrots and garlic; cook 2 minutes longer.  Stir in sweet potatoes, curry, salt, pepper, and remaining water.  Bring to a boil.  Reduce heat; cover and simmer for 10 minutes.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add tomatoes, apple, and brown sugar; cover and cook 10-15 minutes or until apple is tender.  Stir in lentils; heat through.  Serve with rice.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>